[gd_scene format=3]

; The Slag, east of the Kiln (map offset (170, -126)): the volcanic layer's hub, a cavern over a river of slag (SlagBody:
; touching it burns and sets the pilgrim back, plated or not). Basalt pillars rise from the river's bed, each a jump over the
; last; in the middle a stepped mound climbs to the vent of the Chimney (the shortcut home to the Coldstacks), the shrine at
; its west foot. No heat here. West, the Kiln; east, the Ashfall. Two ways down: a pool of coolant walled off west of the
; river whose bottom opens on the Quench (Ballast), and a cracked plug over the walled shaft to the Basalt (the Drill's dive).

